\section{Imports}

We need [[datetime]] for timestamp parsing and [[LearnlogRepo]]
for type annotations in docstrings---the functions accept a repo
instance but do not construct one.
[[collections]] provides the named tuple that carries the results
of the shared log scan (\cref{sec:run-index}).

The recorder owns the commit format, so the field names, the section
markers and the placeholder that stands in for an empty log all come
from \cref{gitrepo} rather than being spelled out a second time here.
Reading a run block (\cref{sec:parse-run-block}) means cutting it at
the same strings the writer used to join it, so importing them is not
tidiness but the only way the two halves can be guaranteed to agree.

