\section{Which commits a reading view shows}
\label{sec:visible-commits}

The filter above works on one message; the reading views page through
a list.
The interactive viewer numbers its position in that list and moves
through it one entry at a time, so a list that still contains a commit
nothing can be drawn for makes the position counter disagree with the
keys---the defect the viewer's placeholder line papers over
(\cref{viewer})---and a student who has listed their log a hundred
times would meet a hundred placeholders.
So the list is filtered before either view sees it, with the same
predicate per commit that [[get_commit_detail]] will apply later.

The decision reads the header messages from [[scan_run_commits]]
(\cref{sec:run-join}) rather than [[git show]], because the scan is
one Git call for the whole log where a show is one per commit.
The trailer merge is not needed for it: [[merge_run_trailers]] folds a
run's results into a block that is already there, and never creates or
removes a block, so whether any block survives is decided by the header
alone.
The rule keeps exactly the commits whose filtered message is not
blank, which is also exactly when [[get_commit_detail]] answers
something rather than [[None]] (\cref{sec:commit-detail}); a commit
with no run block at all---the initial commit---has a message nothing
filters, so it stays in both.
A commit the scan does not know is kept too: hiding what we have not
read would be a guess.
The last test below holds the two readers to that agreement, because a
disagreement shows up as a placeholder nobody asked for or a gap nobody
can see.

<<commits functions>>=
def visible_commits(commits, messages, tag_map=None, *,
                    show_all=False):
    """The commits a reading view lists, in the order given.

    A commit stays when its message still has content after
    the filter :func:`hidden_runs` picks for it.  ``messages``
    is the map from :func:`scan_run_commits`; ``tag_map`` the
    one from :func:`get_tag_map`, which decides which records
    are tagged.
    """
    tag_map = tag_map or {}
    visible = []
    for commit in commits:
        commit_hash = commit["hash"]
        hide = hidden_runs(
            show_all=show_all,
            tagged=bool(tag_map.get(commit_hash)),
        )
        message = messages.get(commit_hash)
        if message is None or filter_runs(message, hide).strip():
            visible.append(commit)
    return visible
@

